<title>NORWAY: Storebrand Q1 profits fall.</title>
<headline>Storebrand Q1 profits fall.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31</p>
<p>				    (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Life, Storebrand share	  154	 vs	   171</p>
<p> Non-life insurance		 24	 vs	   109</p>
<p> Group result			141	 vs	   246</p>
<p> EPS				  0.42	 vs	  0.78</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Norway's biggest insurer is Storebrand ASA. It was expected to post first-quarter group results of 288 million crowns, according to a consensus forecast by seven analysts polled by Reuters.</p>
<p>All analysts said they expected the proposed merger between Storebrand and Christiania Bank og Kreditkasse to come about. A merger between the two would form the biggest financial institution in the country.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
